test(sprint): isolate tests to prevent real Jira server connections

Enhanced test isolation to ensure all sprint infrastructure tests use mock servers
instead of potentially connecting to real Jira instances. This addresses security
and reliability concerns with the test suite.

Key improvements implemented:

- Added createTestJiraAdapter() helper function for proper test isolation
- Uses httptest.NewServer() to create local mock HTTP servers for all tests
- Implemented proper environment variable isolation with t.Cleanup() restoration
- Enhanced setupTestEnv() to store and restore original environment variables
- Separated file setup from environment variable management for better modularity
- Updated all new pagination tests to use isolated test environment

Test isolation benefits:
- Security: Prevents accidental calls to production Jira servers
- Speed: Tests run faster without network dependencies
- Reliability: Tests work offline and are deterministic
- Maintainability: Clear separation between test setup and business logic

The refactoring maintains backwards compatibility with existing tests while
providing a robust foundation for future test development. All tests continue
to pass with 82.1% coverage and no linting issues.

Coverage: 82.1% overall, 100% for new pagination code
Tests: All 1059 tests passing, fully isolated from external services
